{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S2d PS6 (a1471a92fe): PS5 py3.13 CI FAILED — CI runs py3.13.15, my local repro was 3.13.5. Between them, CPython backported gh-75949: _format_usage no longer calls _get_actions_usage_parts (my PS5 override) but a NEW _get_actions_usage_parts_with_split, bypassing the override -> bridge.txt stale again. Lesson: pinning argparse via private-method overrides is version-fragile whack-a-mole (the helper name changed within a single 3.13 patch series). FIX: replaced the private-method override with a robust post-processing override of _format_usage (stable method name across all 3.x) that operates on the RENDERED usage string: split any over-width line ending in ' ...' so the subparsers remainder sits on its own line at the same indent. Depends only on output text + fixed width, not argparse internals. Reproduced CI's exact py3.13.15 locally (homebrew) AND 3.13.5 AND 3.12: gen --check rc=0 on ALL THREE, artifacts byte-identical. Kept _format_action_invocation override (still works on 3.13.15 — 23 core artifacts pass). Both teeth tests hold on 3.12/3.13.15. lint+typecheck+complexity(new=0) clean; 128 parser/gen/b8de/core/advanced passed; held-out 13/13. Pushed PS6; both bots re-triggered."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787291688783912001,"uuid":"c0d70280-4716-41ed-9654-aaeba5287757"}